  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Statistics II: effect of scaling on the mean and standard deviation</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 3.1: Find the mean and standard deviation after every value is multiplied by a and then b is added.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Questions C3 to C5 in Section C of Chapter 2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: combined into one randomised question on a linear change of scale, with diagnostic feedback and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
